# backslash-trailing-comment-par: What does a trailing # comment ending in a backslash do on a par line (XPPAUT 8.2.2)?
# xpp: v@3=2
# pc: ODE0076
# ruling: XPPAUT joins the next line, `x'=a`, into the par line, so it is not an equation and `x'=2` is the only one. PhaseCont ends the par statement at the `#`, swallows `x'=a` into the comment and warns; the model is the same, the path differs (language.md, Lines).
par a=1 # note \
x'=a
x'=2
x(0)=0
aux v=x
@ total=1,dt=0.5,meth=euler
